          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s clear. By the way, I have fatty liver. How does that change which breads are healthy when baking at home in the oven?",
          "user_rubrik": "I have fatty liver. How does that change which breads are healthy when baking at home in the oven?\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When baking bread at home with fatty liver, it's important to choose healthier options that are lower in carbs and higher in fiber. Here are some bread types that are suitable:\n\n1. **Rye Bread**: This is highly recommended for fatty liver due to its high fiber content and lower carb count compared to white bread. You can mix rye flour with whole wheat flour to reduce bitterness and improve taste.\n\n2. **Whole Wheat Bread**: Opt for whole wheat bread as it is less processed than white bread and contains more fiber, which helps with digestion and stabilizes blood sugar levels.\n\n3. **Keto Bread**: If you're comfortable with more advanced baking, consider making keto bread at home. Many store-bought options contain preservatives and additives, so homemade is preferable.\n\n4. **Sprouted Grain Bread**: This type of bread is made from sprouted whole grains, providing more nutrients and being easier on blood sugar levels.\n\nWhen baking, be mindful of the ingredients you use. Avoid added sugars, preservatives, and unhealthy fats. Aim to keep your consumption to 2-3 slices per day for better liver health.",
