      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That seems straightforward! If I have a fatty liver, does it matter which kind of bread I bake at home?",
          "user_rubrik": "I have fatty liver. How does that change which breads are healthy when baking at home in the oven?\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, if you have a fatty liver, it does matter which kind of bread you bake at home. Opt for healthier options like rye bread or whole wheat bread, as they offer more fiber and fewer carbs compared to regular white bread. Rye bread, in particular, is beneficial because it helps with digestion and has a lower impact on blood sugar levels. However, be mindful of the ingredients, as many store-bought breads contain added sugars and preservatives. Baking your own bread allows you to control the ingredients and make healthier choices, which is essential for managing your condition. Aim to keep your consumption moderate, ideally limiting yourself to 2-3 slices per day.",
          "citations": {
