      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s actually helpful, I do eat a lot of raw salads and I'm trying to be healthier! For baking, do I need special equipment for whole grain or rye breads, or can I use my basic oven tools?",
          "user_rubrik": "I have some basic tools for baking bread in the oven at home. What else do I need to get for baking bread in the oven?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "You can absolutely bake whole grain or rye breads using basic oven tools. Essential equipment includes a large mixing bowl, measuring cups and spoons, and a loaf pan or baking sheet. While a Dutch oven or baking stone can enhance the crust and texture, they are not strictly necessary. If you have a cooling rack, it\u2019s helpful for letting the bread cool evenly. For scoring the dough, a simple sharp knife works fine if you don\u2019t have a scoring lame. With your basic tools and some practice, you\u2019ll be able to bake delicious and healthy breads at home!",
