      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "No, that's enough for now! I do want to know: I have some basic tools for baking bread in the oven at home. What else do I need to get for baking bread in the oven?",
          "user_rubrik": "I have some basic tools for baking bread in the oven at home. What else do I need to get for baking bread in the oven?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To bake bread in your oven at home, the basics you'll need are a large mixing bowl for combining ingredients, measuring cups and spoons for accuracy, and a Dutch oven or baking stone to achieve a crisp crust. A bread thermometer helps ensure your bread is fully baked. As you gain experience, consider adding a kitchen scale for precise measurements, a dough scraper and bowl scraper for handling sticky dough, a scoring lame for slashing the dough before baking, and a cooling rack for even cooling after baking. These tools make the process easier and help you achieve more consistent, professional results [clueweb22-en0034-57-14836][clueweb22-en0038-14-07636][clueweb22-en0016-38-16516]. Would you like recommendations for specific brands or models of these tools?",
