          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For individuals with fatty liver, white bread and other refined grain products should be avoided because they are rapidly broken down into sugar, contributing to insulin resistance and worsening liver health. Instead, opt for whole-grain or sprouted grain breads, which are rich in fiber, vitamins, and antioxidants that promote gut and liver health. Baking bread at home allows you to control ingredients, avoid added sugars, and incorporate healthy extras like seeds or nuts. Oatmeal and other whole grains are particularly recommended for their beneficial effects on fatty liver disease. Always choose recipes that use whole-grain flours and minimize added sugars or fats for the healthiest results [clueweb22-en0034-02-17207][clueweb22-en0007-56-05934]. Do you want advice on other foods to support liver health?",
