          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Baking bread in your own oven offers several advantages. First, you have full control over the ingredients, allowing you to avoid additives, preservatives, and excess salt often found in store-bought bread, making it healthier for your family [clueweb22-en0035-25-02171][clueweb22-en0002-94-11906]. Homemade bread is also more cost-effective, with each loaf typically costing less than half of what you'd pay at the store, leading to significant yearly savings [clueweb22-en0016-92-08334][clueweb22-en0018-93-02685]. The taste and aroma of freshly baked bread are unmatched, and you can experiment with different flours, herbs, and add-ins from your garden to create unique flavors. Additionally, baking bread can be a therapeutic and rewarding activity, especially if you enjoy sharing food with guests or family [clueweb22-en0002-94-11906]. Are you interested in tips for making bread with your child?",
