      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Yes, tips for baking bread with my child would be great! Any simple recipes we could try together?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is a good recipe for baking bread in the oven at home?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Baking bread with your child is a great way to teach basic kitchen skills and enjoy quality time together. Simple recipes such as hedgehog rolls, no-yeast naan bread, and easy white bread are perfect for kids. Children can help measure ingredients, mix the dough, and especially enjoy kneading and shaping\u2014turning dough into fun shapes like hedgehogs or rolls makes the process creative and engaging. For example, hedgehog rolls involve forming dough balls and snipping them with scissors to create 'spikes' before baking, while no-yeast naan uses baking powder and is quick to prepare. These activities not only make baking accessible but also encourage kids to try new foods and take pride in their creations. Equipment like digital scales, mixing bowls, and baking trays are helpful, and recipes can be adapted to include herbs from your garden for extra flavor and fun [clueweb22-en0046-69-07832][clueweb22-en0039-16-05190][clueweb22-en0010-18-17848].",
