          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For yeast-based and sourdough breads, your current tools (mixing bowl, measuring cups, baking tray) are enough to get started. A Dutch oven is popular for achieving a crisp crust and good oven spring, but you can also bake directly on a tray or use a loaf pan with great results [clueweb22-en0044-72-01295][clueweb22-en0006-06-06637]. If you want to further improve your bread, consider a baking stone for better heat distribution or a spray bottle to add steam for a crustier loaf. For seeded breads, simply mix pumpkin or sunflower seeds into your dough. Sourdough does not require special equipment, though a proofing basket (banneton) and a sharp blade (lame) for scoring can help with shaping and appearance, but these are optional [clueweb22-en0044-72-01295]. You can start with yeast recipes and move to sourdough as you gain confidence, using the same basic tools.",
