    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That could be interesting! By the way, I have fatty liver. How does that change which breads are healthy when baking at home in the oven?",
          "user_rubrik": "I have fatty liver. How does that change which breads are healthy when baking at home in the oven?\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "If you have fatty liver, you should avoid baking bread with white flour and added sugars, as these refined carbohydrates are rapidly broken down into sugar and can worsen insulin resistance and fatty liver disease [clueweb22-en0034-02-17207][clueweb22-en0037-86-01627]. Instead, opt for whole-grain or sprouted grain flours, which are higher in fiber, antioxidants, and essential nutrients that support liver health and gut health [clueweb22-en0034-02-17207:13]. You can also add seeds or nuts for extra nutrition, and use healthy fats like olive oil instead of butter. These changes make homemade bread a much healthier option for managing fatty liver. Are there specific ingredients you want to include or avoid in your bread?",
          "citations": {
