      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That doesn\u2019t really answer my question. I\u2019m looking for various methods or techniques for baking bread at home\u2014like, what are the different ways to do it? For example, do I need a special oven, or can I use a Dutch oven? Any other equipment or techniques people use?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are ways for baking bread at home?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "You can bake bread at home using various methods and equipment. A Dutch oven is a popular option as it can replicate the steam of a baker's oven, producing a crusty bread. However, you don't necessarily need a Dutch oven. Other alternatives include using a pressure cooker, slow cooker, or even a baking stone or steel with a steam bath in the oven. Some people also use a cast-iron pan or a bread cloche to achieve similar results. You can experiment with different techniques and equipment to find what works best for you and the type of bread you want to make.",
