          "text": "To make homemade rye bread, you can use a mixture of rye flour and standard bread flour for a lighter texture, or all rye flour for a denser, darker bread. To create a steamy environment in your standard oven, you can place a shallow pan of water on the bottom shelf. This will help produce a crusty bread. You can also try scoring the bread before baking to allow it to expand and give it a more artisanal look. Additionally, using a Dutch oven or a baking stone can help create a crispy crust. Keep an eye on the temperature and baking time, and use an instant-read thermometer to ensure the bread is cooked through. With a little practice, you can achieve a delicious homemade rye bread in your standard oven.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0033-51-19484:11": 5.094946384429932,
            "clueweb22-en0042-61-01466:0": 3.8423850536346436,
