      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! I\u2019m curious\u2014if someone has a fatty liver, does that change which kinds of bread they should bake at home to keep it healthy?",
          "user_rubrik": "I have fatty liver. How does that change which breads are healthy when baking at home in the oven?\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "If someone has a fatty liver, it's best to bake bread at home using whole-grain, sprouted, or rye flour. These types of flour are rich in fiber, antioxidants, and essential amino acids, which can help promote liver health and reduce the risk of fatty liver disease. Avoid using refined or processed flours, as they can exacerbate the condition. Additionally, consider reducing or avoiding added sugars and saturated fats in your bread recipes. Opting for healthier ingredients and baking methods can help support liver health and overall well-being. As a beginner, you can start with simple recipes like whole-grain or rye bread, and experiment with different ingredients and flavors as you become more comfortable with bread baking.",
          "citations": {
