          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "When making homemade bread to pair with raw veggies or fresh herbs, consider using ingredients that complement their flavors. For example, you can add fresh or dried herbs like rosemary, thyme, or oregano to your bread dough for a savory flavor. You can also use garlic, olive oil, or lemon juice to enhance the flavor of your bread. Additionally, using whole-grain or sprouted flour can add a nutty flavor and texture that pairs well with raw veggies. If you have a garden with fresh herbs like you do, you can experiment with different herb combinations to find the perfect pairing for your raw salads. This will allow you to create a delicious and healthy accompaniment to your raw veggies.",
