      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Sounds easy enough! I have fatty liver. How does that change which breads are healthy when baking at home in the oven?",
          "user_rubrik": "I have fatty liver. How does that change which breads are healthy when baking at home in the oven?\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "With fatty liver, it's best to opt for breads that are low in carbs and made with whole grains. Rye bread is a good option, as it's lower in carbs and has a more moderate effect on blood sugar levels. You can also try mixing rye flour with whole wheat flour to reduce bitterness. Another option is to make a keto bread, which is low in carbs and can be made with healthy ingredients. When baking at home, be mindful of the ingredients and try to avoid added sugars, preservatives, and unhealthy fats. Moderation is key, so limit your daily bread intake to 2-3 slices. By choosing the right ingredients and being mindful of your portion sizes, you can enjoy healthy bread while managing your fatty liver condition.",
