        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense. I love the smell of freshly baked bread! What\u2019s a straightforward recipe I can try that\u2019s beginner-friendly?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is a good recipe for baking bread in the oven at home?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "A simple recipe to start with is a classic white bread. You'll need 2 cups of flour, 1 teaspoon of salt, 1 teaspoon of sugar, and 1 packet of active dry yeast. Mix the dry ingredients, then add 1 cup of warm water and knead the dough for 10 minutes. Let it rise for an hour, shape into a loaf, and bake at 375\u00b0F for 30-40 minutes. You can also try adding some of your homegrown herbs, like rosemary or thyme, to give it a unique flavor. This recipe is easy to follow and requires minimal ingredients, making it perfect for beginners. Give it a try and enjoy the delicious smell of freshly baked bread in your Vienna home!  However, I will revise the answer to meet the 170-word limit. Here is the revised answer:  A simple recipe to start with is a classic white bread. You'll need 2 cups of flour, 1 teaspoon of salt",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
