        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice! Speaking of healthy, I have fatty liver. How does that change which breads are healthy when baking at home in the oven?\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik": "I have fatty liver. How does that change which breads are healthy when baking at home in the oven?\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For fatty liver, prioritize baking breads high in fiber and low in refined carbohydrates and added sugars. Excellent choices include **rye bread**, often mixed with **whole wheat flour** for better taste (P1, P2, P7, P9). **Keto breads** are also recommended, especially when baked at home to control ingredients (P2, P10). **Sprouted breads** offer more nutrients and a lower impact on blood sugar (P3, P4, P8). Generally, opt for **whole-grain, multi-grain, or stone-ground breads** over white bread (P4, P6, P18, P20). Ensure your recipes use base ingredients like flour, yeast, salt, and water, avoiding added sugars and preservatives (P1, P3).",
