      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great advice. Are there specific herbs I could add to my bread for flavor that would also be good for my health? I grow some in my garden.",
          "user_rubrik": "I have some basic tools for baking bread in the oven at home. What else do I need to get for baking bread in the oven?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "For your homemade bread, considering your fatty liver, you can add herbs for both flavor and health benefits. **Garlic** is excellent as it helps reduce fat and stimulates liver enzymes. **Rosemary** is another great choice, known for its liver-cleansing properties and savory flavor in bread. **Fennel** and **parsley** are also beneficial for liver health and add a nice aroma. Other generally healthy herbs that enhance bread flavor include **sage, thyme, oregano, basil, and dill**.",
          "citations": {
