      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "This is perfect\u2014my garden has rosemary, oregano, and parsley, so I\u2019ll try those. Do you have any tips for getting a good crust when baking bread in a home oven?",
          "user_rubrik": "I have some basic tools for baking bread in the oven at home. What else do I need to get for baking bread in the oven?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "To achieve a good crust when baking bread at home, **steam** is crucial; you can create it by placing a pan of boiling water or ice in your preheating oven. Also, ensure your **oven temperature** is correct and preheated thoroughly. For a crispier crust, consider avoiding enriched doughs and using a **wash of water or oil** before baking. Finally, **cool your bread on a wire rack immediately** after baking to prevent a soggy crust, or even cool it in the oven for extra crispness. Slashing the dough before baking also helps.",
