        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that sounds very doable! If I have a fatty liver, are there things I should adjust in the recipe or when baking bread at home?",
          "user_rubrik": "I have fatty liver. How does that change which breads are healthy when baking at home in the oven?\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Given your fatty liver, it's advisable to adjust the white bread recipe. White bread, with its refined grains and sugar, is generally not recommended as it can worsen fatty liver.\n\nInstead of all-purpose flour, consider using whole wheat or rye flour. Reduce or eliminate the sugar in the recipe. Your current recipe already uses canola or vegetable oil, which is a better choice than butter. If a recipe calls for milk, use fat-free. Always consume bread in moderation, ideally 2-3 slices daily.",
