      {
        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, steaming sounds like something I\u2019d like to try! I have some baking tools already, but I\u2019m not sure if I need anything else for baking bread in the oven. The last answer on this was not helpful. What are the must-have tools for baking bread in an oven?",
          "user_rubrik": "I have some basic tools for baking bread in the oven at home. What else do I need to get for baking bread in the oven?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For baking bread in a home oven, essential tools include a kitchen scale for accurate measurements, mixing bowls, and a dough or bench scraper for handling. To achieve a good crust, especially with steaming, a Dutch oven is highly recommended, or a heavy pan for creating steam. Other useful tools are parchment paper, a cooling rack to prevent a soggy bottom, and a lame or sharp knife for scoring the dough.",
