        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That gives me some options! If I have fatty liver, how does that change which breads are best to bake at home?",
          "user_rubrik": "I have fatty liver. How does that change which breads are healthy when baking at home in the oven?\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For fatty liver, the best breads to bake at home are **rye bread** and **whole wheat bread**. Baking your own allows you to control ingredients, avoiding added sugars and preservatives often found in store-bought options. Rye bread is high in fiber and has fewer carbs than white bread. You can mix rye flour with whole wheat flour to improve taste and density. Whole wheat is also better than white flour due to its fiber content. If you're looking for other options, **keto breads** are good if homemade, though they can be harder to make. Always prioritize whole-grain, complex carbs and eat in moderation (2-3 slices daily).",
