          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That all sounds great. What\u2019s a simple, reliable bread recipe I should try first if I want to get that fresh, crisp crust?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is a good recipe for baking bread in the oven at home?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "try this no \u2011 knead dutch \u2011 oven loaf \u2014 super reliable with a crackly crust. ingredients - 400 g bread or all \u2011 purpose flour ( about 3 1 / 4 cups ) - 1 / 2 tsp instant yeast - 1 1 / 2 tsp fine salt - 300 ml lukewarm water ( about 1 1 / 4 cups ) method 1 ) mix flour, yeast, and salt. add water ; stir until a shaggy dough forms. cover and rest 12 \u2013 18 hours at room temp. 2 ) generously flour the counter ; tip out the sticky dough. with floured hands, shape into a tight ball. 3 ) set on parchment or a silicone bread sling ; cover 30 minutes. meanwhile, place a heavy lidded pot in the oven and preheat to 230 c / 450 f. 4 ) lower dough into the hot pot, cover, and bake 30 minutes. uncover and bake 15 \u2013 20 minutes more, until deep golden and crisp ( about 96 c / 205 f internal ). 5 ) cool on a rack at least 45 minutes before slicing. extras - for even crisper crust, chill the shaped loaf 30 \u2013 60 minutes before baking. - add rosemary or seeds from your garden ; score just",
