      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Super clear, cheers! My tools are pretty basic\u2014just a regular oven, mixing bowls, baking tray, and a basic scale. What else should I get to bake bread in the oven?",
          "user_rubrik": "I have some basic tools for baking bread in the oven at home. What else do I need to get for baking bread in the oven?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "great starting kit already. here \u2019 s what i \u2019 d add, prioritized for crisp, reliable loaves : essential upgrades - 4 \u2013 6 l cast - iron dutch oven with lid ( traps steam for bakery crust ) - parchment paper or a silicone bread sling ( safe loading / unloading ) - instant \u2011 read thermometer ( check 96 \u2013 99\u00b0c / 205 \u2013 210\u00b0f internal doneness ) - bench scraper + flexible dough scraper ( clean handling, easy shaping ) - oven thermometer ( home ovens run hot / cold ) for proofing and shaping - banneton basket ( s ) with liner ( or a colander lined with a floured towel ) - 6 \u2013 8 l clear lidded container for bulk fermentation ( watch dough rise ) for scoring and steam - bread lame or single \u2011 edge razor ( controlled expansion ) - if not using a dutch oven : baking steel / stone + a metal bowl or roasting pan to cover the loaf for the first 20 \u2013 25 min ; spray bottle for misting for specific styles - loaf pan or pullman pan ( sandwich bread ) - perforated baguette pan + linen couche ( baguettes ) nice to have - cooling",
