    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That helps! If I want a recipe for a basic white bread, just enough for a small family, what would you recommend?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is a good recipe for baking bread in the oven at home?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "great \u2014 try this simple, family - sized basic white loaf ( makes one 10 \" \u00d74. 5 \" loaf ) : ingredients - 2 tbsp fresh yeast ( \u224815 \u2013 20 g ) - 300 ml warm water ( about 1\u00bc cups ) - 1 / 8 cup sugar ( \u224825 g ) - 1 tsp salt ( \u22485 g ) - 1 tbsp vegetable oil ( 15 ml ) - 3 \u2013 3\u00bd cups plain / all \u2011 purpose flour ( \u2248375 \u2013 437 g ) steps 1. dissolve yeast in warm water, stir in sugar. 2. add oil, salt and most of the flour. mix to a shaggy dough. 3. turn onto floured surface and knead ~ 8 \u2013 10 minutes until smooth ( or use mixer until elastic ). add remaining flour if too sticky. 4. place in a lightly oiled bowl, cover, let rise until doubled ( about 1 \u2013 2 hours ). 5. punch down, shape into a loaf, put in greased loaf pan. cover and prove ~ 30 \u2013 60 minutes. 6. preheat oven to 200\u00b0c. bake 25 \u2013 35 minutes until golden and internal temp ~ 95\u00b0c ( or hollow sound ). 7.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0019-88-11991:0": -3.809443950653076,
