          "text": "yes \u2014 having fatty liver means being more careful with breads. practical points : - limit portions. bread is high in carbs ; keep servings small ( start with 1 \u2013 2 slices / day ) or treat it as an occasional food while you improve liver markers and weight. - avoid refined / sweet breads. no white, enriched, sweetened, or pastry - style loaves ( donuts, brioche, sugar - added rolls ). - prefer lower \u2011 glycemic or alternative flours at home : rye, buckwheat, quinoa, amaranth, or flours like soy / pea. sourdough fermentation often gives a gentler glycemic response. - try grain \u2011 free or \u201c keto \u201d homemade breads ( almond / coconut / pea flour ) if you want minimal carbs \u2014 easier to control when home - baked. store \u2011 bought keto breads are hit - or - miss. - boost protein / fat and fiber in the loaf ( seeds, nuts, eggs, herbs ) to slow glucose spikes and make slices more satisfying. - if you have diabetes or very fatty liver, some clinicians recommend avoiding all grains / sugar for a period ( 3",
