          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s really useful. I have some basic tools for baking bread in the oven at home. What else do I need to get for baking bread in the oven? The last answer wasn\u2019t really helpful.",
          "user_rubrik": "I have some basic tools for baking bread in the oven at home. What else do I need to get for baking bread in the oven?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Good \u2014 here\u2019s a focused checklist of tools that make oven bread baking easier and more reliable, ranked by impact so you can prioritize purchases:  High-impact (buy first) - Digital kitchen scale (accurate to 1 g): consistency beats cups.   - Instant-read thermometer: perfect doneness (internal ~95\u00b0C for white loaf).   - Dutch oven (cast iron or ceramic, 4\u20136 qt): easiest way to get bakery steam, great crust.   - Bench/dough scraper and bowl scraper: shaping, cutting and cleaning sticky doughs.    Very helpful - Lame or sharp razor blade: clean, controlled scoring for oven spring.   - Parchment paper and a good serrated bread knife.   - Banneton (proofing basket) or bowl + linen: keeps shape and creates a nice skin.   - Baking stone or steel (optional): better bottom crust when baking uncovered.    Nice-to-have - Oven thermometer, spray bottle or small roasting pan (for creating steam), cooling rack, stand mixer (if you prefer less hand kneading).  If you want, tell me what you already own and I\u2019ll suggest the next one to buy.",
